From 66e97f88671f983f72d87085d005cd3776296304 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nick <nickjb78@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 4 Jul 2026 11:51:23 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] fix(focus): honor explicit focuswindow dispatches while an
 exclusive layer surface is mapped

rawWindowFocus refuses any window focus while m_exclusiveLSes is
non-empty. That guard is right for implicit focus changes (hover,
mouse motion, map-time focus stealing), but it also eats explicit
`dispatch focuswindow` requests, which carry direct user intent.

Concrete breakage: GTK task switchers (hyprshell-style Alt+Tab
overlays) map their picker as a keyboard-exclusive layer surface and
dispatch focuswindow for the chosen window while the overlay is still
mapped. The dispatch returns "ok" but is silently dropped, and when
the overlay unmaps, focus falls back to the previously-active window,
so the switch never happens.

Allow FOCUS_REASON_DISPATCH_FOCUSWINDOW through the exclusive-ls
refusal. The sessionlock refusal above it is untouched, a locked
session still refuses all window focus. Implicit reasons (FFM, click,
desktop state changes) still defer to the exclusive layer.

Verified with a nested A/B probe: two clients + wofi (exclusive
keyboard) mapped, `dispatch focuswindow` on the unfocused client.
Unpatched: activewindow unchanged. Patched: activewindow moves to
the target.
---
 src/desktop/state/FocusState.cpp | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/desktop/state/FocusState.cpp b/src/desktop/state/FocusState.cpp
index 702b02c4..9671ef2a 100644
--- a/src/desktop/state/FocusState.cpp
+++ b/src/desktop/state/FocusState.cpp
@@ -104,7 +104,10 @@ void CFocusState::rawWindowFocus(PHLWINDOW pWindow, eFocusReason reason, SP<CWLS
             return;
         }
 
-        if (!g_pInputManager->m_exclusiveLSes.empty()) {
+        // explicit focuswindow dispatches carry user intent (task switchers dispatch
+        // while their own exclusive overlay is still mapped); sessionlock is already
+        // refused above, so only implicit focus changes defer to the exclusive ls
+        if (!g_pInputManager->m_exclusiveLSes.empty() && reason != FOCUS_REASON_DISPATCH_FOCUSWINDOW) {
             Log::logger->log(Log::DEBUG, "Refusing a keyboard focus to a window because of an exclusive ls");
             return;
         }
